Explanation of the change:

1. In the loop inside `renderWorlds`, we build up `currentTransform_` as a combination of the fresh projection (`makeProjectionTransform`) plus the world offset plus the inverse of the projection used when the buffers were built.
2. By swapping the calls to `multiplyTransform(…, invertRenderTransform_)` and `translateTransform(… world * worldWidth, 0)`, any per‐feature quad offsets (including the rotate‐with‐view rotation) get applied first in clip space—i.e. before the non-uniform X/Y scale from the projection goes on. That restores the correct 1:1 aspect for rotated symbols even when your canvas isn’t square.
